        "contact": {
          "name": "IP2Location API Support",
          "url": "https://www.ip2location.io"
        },
        "description": "The IP2Location API provides a RESTful interface for determining the geographical location of users based on their IP addresses in real time. It supports both IPv4 and IPv6 lookups, returning detailed information such as country, city, and coordinates without requiring an API key for up to 500 queries daily.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production server",
            "url": "https://api.ip2location.io"
          }
        ],
        "termsOfService": "https://www.ip2location.io",
        "title": "IP Geolocation API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Resolve IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to country, region, city, coordinates, and network info",
        "homepage": "https://www.ip2location.io",
        "docs_url": "https://www.ip2location.io/ip2location-documentation",
        "license_short": "Proprietary service; free keyless tier with daily query cap, paid plans for higher volume.",
        "license_md": "- Operated by [IP2Location.io](https://www.ip2location.io) under its [Terms of Service](https://www.ip2location.io/terms-of-service).\n- Keyless access is rate-limited; higher tiers require account signup and an API key.\n- Check the IP2Location terms before redistributing or caching geolocation results.",
        "about_md": "[IP2Location.io](https://www.ip2location.io) is a geolocation lookup service that maps an IPv4 or IPv6 address to location and network attributes. The public REST endpoint at `https://api.ip2location.io/` can be queried without credentials for light usage, with paid plans unlocking richer fields and higher quotas.\n\nWhat you get from a lookup:\n\n- Location: country code and name, region, city, ZIP code, latitude/longitude, and time zone.\n- Network: ASN, AS name, and (on higher plans) ISP, domain, net speed, and usage type.\n- Optional fields on paid plans: mobile carrier (MCC/MNC), proxy/fraud detection, currency, and language.\n\nOperational notes: keyless callers are capped at roughly 500-1,000 queries per day (resetting at 00:00 UTC); authenticated calls accept the key either as a `key` query parameter or as a `Bearer` token in the `Authorization` header. The service returns JSON by default and also supports XML and a `lang` parameter for localized country/region names. CORS is disabled on the public endpoint.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "get_ip_geolocation": "Looks up the geolocation and network metadata for an IPv4 or IPv6 address via `GET /?ip={ip}` on `api.ip2location.io`, optionally accepting `key`, `format`, and `lang` query parameters."
        },
